Data
├── HasRole
│   ├── when the account has been granted the role
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── when the account has not been granted the role
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── when the role has never been granted to any account
│   │   └── it should return false
│   └── when the account is the zero address
│       └── it should return false
└── RequireRole
    ├── when the account has the role
    │   └── it should not revert
    └── when the account does not have the role
        └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}

Admin
├── GetRoleAdmin
│   ├── when the role has never had an explicit admin set
│   │   └── it should return the default admin role
│   └── when the role has an explicit admin set
│       └── it should return the stored admin role
└── SetRoleAdmin
    ├── when the caller has the current admin role for the target role
    │   ├── it should update the admin role mapping
    │   └── it should emit a {RoleAdminChanged} event
    └── when the caller does not have the current admin role for the target role
        └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}

Grant
└── GrantRole
    ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
    │   ├── and the account does not yet have the role
    │   │   ├── it should set hasRole[account][role] to true
    │   │   ├── it should emit a {RoleGranted} event
    │   │   └── it should return true from the module function
    │   └── and the account already has the role
    │       ├── it should leave hasRole[account][role] unchanged
    │       ├── it should not emit an additional {RoleGranted} event
    │       └── it should return false from the module function
    └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
        └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}

Revoke
└── RevokeRole
    ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
    │   ├── and the account currently has the role
    │   │   ├── it should set hasRole[account][role] to false
    │   │   ├── it should clear roleExpiry[account][role]
    │   │   ├── it should emit a {RoleRevoked} event
    │   │   └── it should return true from the module function
    │   └── and the account does not have the role
    │       ├── it should leave hasRole[account][role] unchanged
    │       └── it should return false from the module function
    └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
        └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}

Renounce
└── RenounceRole
    ├── when msg.sender equals the account
    │   ├── and the account currently has the role
    │   │   ├── it should set hasRole[account][role] to false
    │   │   ├── it should clear roleExpiry[account][role]
    │   │   └── it should emit a {RoleRevoked} event
    │   └── and the account does not have the role
    │       └── it should be a no-op and not emit any event
    └── when msg.sender does not equal the account
        └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedSender}

Batch
└── Grant
│   └── GrantRoleBatch
│       ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
│       │   ├── and the accounts array is empty
│       │   │   └── it should succeed without emitting any events
│       │   └── and the accounts array is non-empty
│       │       ├── for each account without the role
│       │       │   ├── it should set hasRole[account][role] to true
│       │       │   └── it should emit a {RoleGranted} event
│       │       └── for each account that already has the role
│       │           └── it should not change storage or emit {RoleGranted}
│       └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
│           └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
└── Revoke
    └── RevokeRoleBatch
        ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
        │   ├── and the accounts array is empty
        │   │   └── it should succeed without emitting any events
        │   └── and the accounts array is non-empty
        │       ├── for each account with the role
        │       │   ├── it should set hasRole[account][role] to false
        │       │   ├── it should clear roleExpiry[account][role]
        │       │   └── it should emit a {RoleRevoked} event
        │       └── for each account that does not have the role
        │           └── it should not change storage or emit {RoleRevoked}
        └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
            └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}

RoleHierarchy
├── when a role’s admin role is itself
│   └── an account with the role should be able to grant and revoke that same role
├── when roles form a linear hierarchy (role1 admin is DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, role2 admin is role1, role3 admin is role2)
│   ├── only DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE holders can grant role1
│   ├── only role1 holders can grant role2
│   └── only role2 holders can grant role3
└── when roles form a circular admin relationship
    └── each grant or revoke must still satisfy the immediate admin-role check

Pausable
├── IsRolePaused
│   ├── when the role has not been paused
│   │   └── it should return false
│   └── when the role has been paused
│       └── it should return true
├── PauseRole
│   ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
│   │   ├── it should set pausedRoles[role] to true
│   │   ├── it should emit a {RolePaused} event
│   │   └── when the role is already paused and PauseRole is called again
│   │       └── it should remain paused (idempotent)
│   └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
│       ├── on the facet surface it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
│       └── on the module surface it should follow the current split implementation semantics
├── UnpauseRole
│   ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
│   │   ├── it should set pausedRoles[role] to false
│   │   ├── it should emit a {RoleUnpaused} event
│   │   └── when the role is already unpaused and UnpauseRole is called again
│   │       └── it should remain unpaused (idempotent)
│   └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
│       ├── on the facet surface it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
│       └── on the module surface it should follow the current split implementation semantics
├── RequireRoleNotPaused
│   ├── when the account does not have the role
│   │   └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
│   ├── when the account has the role and the role is paused
│   │   └── it should revert with {AccessControlRolePaused}
│   └── when the account has the role and the role is not paused
│       └── it should not revert
└── PauseUnpauseCycles
    └── when multiple pause and unpause cycles are performed for the same role
        └── it should end in the unpaused state when last action is unpause

Temporal
├── Data
│   ├── GetRoleExpiry
│   │   ├── when no expiry has been set for the role assignment
│   │   │   └── it should return 0
│   │   └── when an expiry has been set for the role assignment
│   │       └── it should return the stored expiry timestamp
│   ├── IsRoleExpired
│   │   ├── when no expiry is set and the account does not have the role
│   │   │   └── it should return true
│   │   ├── when no expiry is set and the account has the role
│   │   │   └── it should return false
│   │   ├── when an expiry is set in the future
│   │   │   └── it should return false
│   │   └── when block.timestamp is greater than or equal to the stored expiry
│   │       └── it should return true
│   └── RequireValidRole
│       ├── when the account does not have the role
│       │   └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
│       ├── when the account has the role and no expiry is set
│       │   └── it should not revert
│       ├── when the account has the role and the expiry is in the future
│       │   └── it should not revert
│       └── when the account has the role and block.timestamp is greater than or equal to the stored expiry
│           └── it should revert with {AccessControlRoleExpired}
├── Grant
│   └── GrantRoleWithExpiry
│       ├── when the caller has the admin role for the target role
│       │   ├── and the expiry is in the future
│       │   │   ├── it should grant the role if it is not already granted
│       │   │   ├── it should set the expiry timestamp
│       │   │   └── it should emit a {RoleGrantedWithExpiry} event
│       │   └── and the expiry is less than or equal to block.timestamp
│       │       └── it should revert with {AccessControlRoleExpired}
│       └── when the caller does not have the admin role for the target role
│           └── it should revert with {AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount}
ExportSelectors
└── for each AccessControl facet (data, admin, grant, revoke, renounce, batch, pausable, temporal)
    └── it should return an abi.encodePacked list of that facet's external function selectors in the expected order
